  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 3e4b5683c1ea36345958694d590b6436, type: 3}
  m_Name: COC3_Quiz_LO1_UserAccess_Q08
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::QuizQuestionData
  questionText: What does a GLOBAL group scope mean?
  choices:
  - It can hold accounts from this domain and be used anywhere in the forest
  - It is visible to every computer on the internet
  - It holds every account in the domain automatically
  - It can only be used on the domain controller
  correctChoiceIndex: 0
  points: 10
  explanation: Global is the normal scope for a group of people from one domain.
    Domain local is for granting access within one domain; universal spans a whole
    forest.
